<newsitem itemid="209814" id="root" date="1996-11-22" xml:lang="en">
<title>SINGAPORE: Times Publishing full year net profit up.</title>
<headline>Times Publishing full year net profit up.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year ended August 31 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore $ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   24.08	 vs	19.44</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	19.80	 vs	16.00</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)	    6.00	 vs	 6.00</p>
<p>    Turnover		    508.02	 vs     479.19</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	     35.42	 vs	31.26</p>
<p>    Associates		    0.48	 vs	 0.55 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax			    11.08	 vs	10.60</p>
<p>    Interest on borrowings    1.97	 vs	 1.04</p>
<p>    Depreciation		 17.15	 vs	16.16</p>
<p>    Minorities	   (loss) 0.74	 vs	 0.68 (loss)</p>
<p>Div register/pay  -  January 29, 1997 / February 5, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Times Publishing Ltd said a significant part of the increase in its turnover came from its subsidiaries in Singapore and Australia.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
